% A group is the set of rows over the body's named variables.  Over
% edge(a, b) and edge(a, c), the body edge(a, Y) has two rows, one for each
% Y, and the body edge(a, _) has one row of no columns, as the query
% edge(a, _)? prints one empty row.
edge(a, b). edge(a, c).

neighbours(N) :- N = count { edge(a, Y) }.
connected(N) :- N = count { edge(a, _) }.

neighbours(N)?
connected(N)?
edge(a, _)?
